  "decision": "Main inherits this exact CSS-query fix from its advertised minimum CDK22.1.7: the actual insertion string strips every literal brace with the same expression as the full original hunk. Reviewed owned direct and BreakpointObserver/high-contrast callers use fixed queries. Actual public MediaMatcher in packed zoneful Chromium confirms a valid query works, the malformed query has no marker effect and its insertion attempt has braces removed. No owned sanitizer, private API or CDK fork is introduced. This is a bounded disposition of this SHA on main, not a full security clearance;21.x21.2.14 retains raw insertion and reproduced injection, so its security review remains open.",
